Creatine Kinase Elevation in Calliophis Envenoming

1. Summary
(A) Direct myotoxicity, principally from PLA2. Reasonably supported. PLA2 dominates the proteome by mass, whole venom is demonstrably myotoxic in mice, and PLA2 myotoxicity is well characterised across elapids.
(B) Channel-mediated myotoxicity from calliotoxin at NaV1.4. Speculative, and weakened by the abundance finding above.
They are not mutually exclusive, and they predict different EMG findings.

